# mv — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R50 (Wave 2)
# Doc:  design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.7 in the paideia-os repo.
#
# mv moves one path onto another. Every M1 invocation degenerates to
# a same-directory rename — src and dst share a parent, so the two
# write authorities collapse into ONE KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <parent>).
# M2 splits the two out again for the cross-directory case (rename
# opens ONE TXN that touches BOTH parents; the caps.decl still names
# them separately so exec-time cap_manifest_verify catches a caller
# that forgot to hand down one side or the other).
#
# The M1 baseline is:
#
#   * KIND_USER (self)             — identity root. mv checks the
#                                    caller's KIND_USER tail before it
#                                    touches an inode (D3 audit-first,
#                                    R48.M1 KIND_USER = 0x190 substrate
#                                    at paideia-os
#                                    src/kernel/core/cap/kind_user.pdx).
#
#   * KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)   — baseline pipe substrate (R20b,
#                                    base kind 5). Consumers use it
#                                    for stdout/stderr rendering. M3
#                                    wires libpdx-semantic-pipe on top
#                                    for MoveRecord[] emission.
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <src-parent>) — write authority on the
#                                    directory that holds src. M1 uses
#                                    it to unlink the source dirent
#                                    inside the TXN.
#                                    KIND_PDXFS_FILE = 0x195 (R42
#                                    substrate, landed in paideia-os
#                                    commit 411ad0e).
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <dst-parent>) — write authority on the
#                                    directory that will hold dst. M1
#                                    uses it to link the target dirent
#                                    inside the SAME TXN. For same-dir
#                                    rename src-parent == dst-parent
#                                    and the two caps refer to the
#                                    same underlying dir inode; the
#                                    caps.decl still names them
#                                    separately so M2's cross-dir path
#                                    is a code change, not a manifest
#                                    change.
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_TXN (invoke, mint) — transaction authority so mv can
#                                    open one TXN, thread the unlink
#                                    + link through it, and commit
#                                    atomically. invoke is used for
#                                    query ops on an existing txn;
#                                    mint is what mv needs to open a
#                                    new one at invocation.
#                                    KIND_PDXFS_TXN = 0x196 (R42
#                                    substrate).
#
# --- placeholder: elevate-broker binding -------------------------------
# Reserved for the M3-004 wire-up (cross-user-boundary destination).
# Uncomment when libpdx-elevate.M3 is in-tree and the paideia-os
# elevate broker (R48.M7 at src/kernel/core/ipc/elevate_broker.pdx)
# is running. M1's mv never crosses user boundaries — a mv onto a
# path whose parent belongs to another user is refused with
# MV_ARG_UNSUP at exec until M3.
#
#   - KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL (invoke, svc.elevate-broker)   # 0x191 R48.M7
requires:
  - KIND_USER (self)
  - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <src-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <dst-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_TXN (invoke, mint)

# Declared output schemas — the semantic-pipe schema records mv emits
# on stdout. M1 emits none (a successful same-dir rename is silent
# unless -v is given, in which case a plain-text `mv <src> <dst>`
# line goes to stdout via the tty). M3 introduces MoveRecord[] via
# libpdx-semantic-pipe with was_rename / was_cross_device flags.
declares_output_schemas: (none)
